      "body": "AgentLayer's x402 skill documents a real buyer loop: `x402_preview_request` parses an unpaid `PAYMENT-REQUIRED` header, then `x402_pay_request` can execute when the active backend is Base (`eip155:8453`) or Solana mainnet. The wallet maps `base` → `eip155:8453` and already recognizes Base USDC. Public docs still describe EVM as prepare-oriented; the skill says Base can pay. A live independent 402 is useful either way.\n\nI work on zFinia (https://zfinia.com). This is not a request to add an origin to `KNOWN_X402_ORIGINS`, list us on Bazaar/Agentic Market, endorse the product, or buy anything.\n\nIf you want a cheap **Base mainnet exact** regression target for preview (and pay, if Base execute is on), this existing route is live:\n\n- `POST https://api.zfinia.com/x402/v1/accessibility-contrast-calculator`\n- Network `eip155:8453`, scheme `exact`, amount `1000` atomic USDC (`$0.001`)\n- Unpaid POST returns HTTP 402 with a `PAYMENT-REQUIRED` header (x402 v2 `accepts[]`)\n- Catalog: https://api.zfinia.com/.well-known/x402.json\n\nBody that matches the live 402:\n\n```json\n{\"foreground\":\"#000000\",\"background\":\"#ffffff\",\"large_text\":false}\n```\n\nAfter independent buyer settlement and retry, the paid JSON includes `contrast_ratio: 21`.\n\nzFinia MCP at https://api.zfinia.com/mcp is challenge-handoff only. It will not sign or pay. The paid resource is the HTTP POST above, which matches `x402_preview_request` / `x402_pay_request` better than an MCP session.\n\nIf you already have a preferred Base demo host, ignore this. Reply here or to support@zfinia.com if the 402 terms are incompatible with preview selection (CAIP-2 vs legacy `base`, `amount` vs `maxAmountRequired`, or header name).",
