      "body": "This PR is a little research experiment to figure out how hard it is to include x402 payments for sharing keys in indexd.\r\nThe goal would be to support configuring arbitrary facilitators instead of locking users into using a specific third party service. \r\n\r\nIt should allow users to attach a price to a sharing key that has to be paid once to unlock it and make it usable. Payment is handled by a middleware that the 4 sharing endpoints are wrapped it that currently require a sharing key for authentication.\r\n\r\nNext steps involve deploying an indexer on the testnet, creating a branch with support for this to the go sdk and then see if this works with testnet USDC.\r\n\r\nThe client purposefully doesn't handle any payments. It will let the caller check whether payment is required and the required price but the payment has to be created outside the client library and then passed to it.",
