        "merged_at": null
      },
      "body": "Syncs `main` with `x402-foundation/x402` (upstream), which it has not tracked since **June 17, 2026**.\n\n| | commit | date |\n|---|---|---|\n| upstream `main` | `e398a9e5` | 2026-08-28 |\n| this fork's `main` | `17bd7e59` | 2026-06-17 |\n\n**200 commits, 2,221 files.**\n\n### Why this is safe\n\n- This fork's `main` is a **strict ancestor** of upstream `main` — it carries **zero unique commits**. Nothing here is overwritten or lost.\n- All **200/200 commits are signature-verified**.\n- The branch head is byte-identical to upstream `e398a9e5`.\n\n### Heaviest areas\n\n| path | files |\n|---|---|\n| `typescript/site` | 539 |\n| `typescript/packages` | 491 |\n| `python/x402` | 220 |\n| `e2e/servers` | 187 |\n| `go/mechanisms` | 155 |\n\nIncludes 27 release/version commits across the npm, Go, and PyPI packages.\n\n### Merge note\n\nThis is a fork-sync, so a **fast-forward** would be ideal — it keeps `main` identical to upstream and leaves future syncs trivial. The org ruleset on the default branch permits only `squash` and `rebase`, both of which rewrite these 200 commits into new SHAs and permanently diverge this fork's history from upstream. Merging that way is fine for getting current, but it means subsequent syncs will need the same treatment rather than a clean fast-forward.\n\nThe durable fix is a `bypass_actor` on org ruleset `16107824` so `POST /repos/solana-foundation/x402/merge-upstream` can fast-forward `main` directly. Without it this fork has no clean sync path.\n\n### Open PRs\n\nThe SVM stack (#1–#4) is based on July/August upstream commits and is unaffected by this sync, though those branches will sit behind `main` afterward. #1 (`feat/svm-recent-blockhash`) targets `main` and may want a rebase once this lands.\n",
