      "body": "Hi @smartflowproai-lang,\n\nYour x402 observatory on Base (measuring real vs wash agent-payment flows) is the perfect complement to Kuberna. We were the *first external team* through the Tollbeam x402 rail:\n\n- **5 settled payments on Base mainnet** via `TollbeamClient.payAndFetch` on Tollbeam's production rail\n- **128/128 sponsored UserOp burst, 0 failures, on Base testnet** (`base-sepolia`) — harness reports in `reports/tollbeam-base-sepolia-burst-*.json`\n\nClarifying the rail split explicitly: the paid `payAndFetch` rail settles on mainnet; the UserOp harness runs `base-sepolia` by design, so the paymaster path is exercised without a funded wallet spending anything during development. The burst reports are testnet and should be read as such.\n\nTwo issues match your domain exactly:\n- **#63** — Integrate Tollbeam sponsored UserOps into the SDK for gasless agent execution\n- **#64** — Add provider-failover scenario to the Tollbeam harness (Alchemy vs Pimlico drop)\n\nYour live Base data would validate both. Interested?\n\nContributing guide: https://github.com/kawacukennedy/kuberna-labs/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md",
